# Artifacts the Docker milestone tests write into the repo through the bind
# mount. `berth dev` and several milestones mount the workspace root at
# /workspace, and apps/filesystem's declared write path IS /workspace — so a
# test that exercises an in-scope write lands a real file here. Ignored rather
# than cleaned up afterwards because a test that fails midway never reaches its
# own cleanup, and these were committed once already by a stray `git add -A`.
# (capability-enforcement.mjs, multi-app-milestone.mjs)
/allowed.txt
/concurrent-inside-*.txt
/escape-read-link
/escape-write-link
/multi-app-test.txt
/packages/docker-orchestrator/test/fixtures/boundary-app-b/b-owned.txt
/packages/docker-orchestrator/test/fixtures/boundary-app-b/pwned-by-a.txt
/packages/docker-orchestrator/test/fixtures/boundary-app-b/written-for-c.txt

# A macOS $TMPDIR path ("/var/folders/...") that lost its leading slash and got
# recreated relative to the repo root. Nothing in the current tree does this,
# but the shape is easy to reintroduce and trivially easy to `git add -A`.
/var/
